  "articleBody": "It's easy to look at a small patch of mold on drywall and think, \"I'll just paint over that,\" but that's a mistake you'll regret. Ignoring visible mold or that musty odor after a storm is one of the biggest errors homeowners make. Here's why you need to address it head-on. First, mold often indicates there's still moisture present, which means the problem isn't truly resolved. Second, hidden mold or wet insulation behind the drywall can be a significant health hazard and cause further structural damage. Third, starting repairs before you're absolutely sure the wall cavity is dry can lead to recurring mold and wasted effort. If you've got mold, it often means the drywall has been wet for more than 48 hours, pushing it into replacement territory. Don't risk it; getting a professional opinion can help you assess the full extent of the issue and ensure your home is safe and sound.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}